            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> `vim.fs.watch(patterns, opts, handler)` subscribes to one `fd`-handler-style glob/list of globs\n>\n> ... A shared broker \n\nAnytime a subscription + registry is needed, it's a strong signal that the feature should be a core event (autocmd). The event/autocmd system exists for that purpose. It has a UI (`:au`), scopes (buf/win), patterns, etc. Maybe we should add a builtin `debounce` for events too.",
